.TH VFORK 2 "January 2026" "Substrate Kernel" "System Calls Manual"
.SH NAME
vfork \- create a child process and block parent
.SH LIBRARY
Standard C library (libc, -lc)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B #include <unistd.h>
.PP
.BI "pid_t vfork(void);"
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B vfork()
creates a new process, just like
.BR fork (2).
However, the parent process is suspended until the child terminates or calls
.BR execve (2).
The child shares the parent's memory, so it must not modify memory (except for specific variables) or return from the calling function.
.SH RETURN VALUE
On success, the PID of the child process is returned in the parent, and 0 is returned in the child. On failure, -1 is returned.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR fork (2),
.BR execve (2)
